1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,960
Next I forced myself to journal out what a high value friend looks like to me.
接下来，她逼自己写日记，想清楚自己所说的高价值朋友，对自己而言究竟是什么样。

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:09,480
What do I actually want what do I expect what are my standards.
自己到底想要什么、期待什么，标准又是什么。

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:15,440
Most times we don't know what a good friend is because we've always been conditioned to just like make friends with the person you sit next to in school.
她觉得，人们往往只是习惯了和学校里坐在旁边的人交朋友，所以并不清楚自己认为什么是好朋友。

4
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,880
But as you get older and you begin growing into your own person.
但随着年龄增长，你会渐渐发展出自己的个性与想法。

5
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:21,920
This ensures that you're not just settling for anything.
她认为，想清楚这些能避免自己随便接受任何一种关系。

6
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:27,160
You sat there and wrote out okay I want my friend to be kind I want her to be giving I want her to be open minded.
她会写下：希望朋友善良、慷慨，也能保持开放心态。

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:30,280
I want us to be able to disagree and be honest with each other and come back together.
她希望朋友之间能够意见不同、坦诚相待，之后仍然可以重归于好。

8
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:34,480
There to be no jealousy this is what I expect out of a friend.
她也希望没有嫉妒，这就是她对朋友的期待。

9
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,680
I had a little weird encounter with a girl on instagram.
她回忆，自己曾在 Instagram 上和一个女孩有过让她觉得奇怪的接触。

10
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,520
She was like oh girl we should hang out we should be cool we should be friends.
那个女孩突然说，她们应该一起出去玩、熟悉起来、做朋友。

11
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,280
Out of nowhere I was a little skeptical at first.
对方突然这样说，她起初有点怀疑。

12
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:45,320
She was just like adding me I'm like okay we should be cool we should hang out maybe we should study together I see you go to school.
对方继续加她、邀她一起玩，还提议一起学习，说自己看到她也在上学。

13
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,880
I was like okay cool we can definitely do that.
她回应说，可以，当然能一起学习。

14
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:51,920
But mind you she had a friend group and a lot of people that was a part of her friend group was my mutuals on instagram.
不过，那女孩有自己的朋友圈，其中不少人也和作者在 Instagram 上互相关注。

15
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:56,320
So as I was watching their stories I was seeing that they was going out to eat without her.
作者看他们的动态时，发现那些人出去吃饭却没有带上那个女孩。

16
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,960
They was doing little events without her.
他们也会不带她参加一些小活动；字幕保留非标准语法。

17
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:01,000
So as I'm seeing that then I look at her in my dms talking about some.
看到这些后，作者又看见那个女孩在私信里向自己发出邀请。

18
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,880
We should be friends we should be cool.
私信里说的仍是：我们应该做朋友，应该熟悉起来。

19
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,440
Girl you was never trying to get at me you was never trying to see what I was talking about.
作者因此觉得，对方原本并没有真正想认识她、了解她是什么样的人。

20
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,160
You was never trying to be my little one two friend.
她觉得，对方之前也没有想和自己发展一段交情；这里的俚语说法待原声复核。

21
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:11,479
But now because your friends are treating you weird you think I'm going to be your seconds hell no.
作者认为，对方现在是被原来的朋友冷落了，才把自己当成备选；她强烈拒绝这个位置。

22
00:01:11,479 --> 00:01:15,520
No no thank you I'm okay I don't want to be your seconds go get cool with your friends.
她说自己没兴趣当备选，让对方回去和原来的朋友和好。

23
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:18,320
You don't want a friend you just want to make it seem like you cool without them now.
她判断，对方并不是真的想找朋友，只想表现得像是离开原朋友圈也过得很好。

24
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:22,070
And then you posting quotes like never gave up to make anybody to be a good friend.
她接着提到对方发的一段关于朋友的引语；这里自动字幕句意残缺，无法据此确认原话。

25
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:25,200
Because I had already written a list of type of friend that I want.
因为她已经列过自己想结交什么样的朋友。

26
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,800
I want no friend who already got messed I'm living a peaceful life over here.
她不想要一开始就带着是非的关系，说自己现在生活得很平静；字幕中的 messed 用词待核验。

27
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,920
And then you hang around weird people just not the nicest.
她又说，对方身边那些人看起来古怪、也不太友善，这是她的主观印象。

28
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,800
Something in you connects with them on a certain level that I don't want to be a part of.
她觉得，对方在某个层面认同那些人，而她不想卷入其中。

29
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,800
It wasn't genuine.
她因此觉得，这个交友邀请并不真诚。

30
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,160
If I was at a point where I wasn't content with my alone time and just spending time with myself and learning who I was.
如果她当时并不满足于独处、花时间认识自己，她可能会做出不同反应。

31
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:43,320
Knowing that the right group of friends will come.
现在，她相信适合自己的朋友以后会出现。

32
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:46,080
I was like yeah girl let's do that even if I seen red flags.
否则她可能即使看见警示信号，也会说好呀，一起玩吧；字幕保留非标准时态。

33
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:49,640
It's so crazy cuz I've had so many different little weird encounters when it comes to friends.
她说，关于交朋友，自己遇到过不少这样的奇怪情况。

34
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:52,960
But this one girl reached out to me god who was known in our city he was having a birthday party.
接着她讲另一次经历：一位当地有人认识的人要办生日派对；字幕中的 god 疑似误识别，待核验。

35
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,110
He was posting about a birthday party for like weeks and weeks.
那人提前好几个星期，就一直在发生日派对的消息。

36
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:58,320
The night before his birthday party one of the girls that was going she going to reach out to me.
到了派对前一晚，一个要参加的女孩才来联系她。

37
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,110
Like hey girl do you want to come to the party with me.
那个女孩问她，要不要一起去参加派对。

38
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:03,790
Never talked to this girl a day in my life never met her girl are you cool.
作者说，自己从来没跟这个女孩说过话，也从没见过她，因此觉得很不对劲。

39
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,640
My mom always taught me a late invite is not a real invitation.
她说，妈妈一直教她，迟来的邀请不是真正的邀请；这是她家庭里的判断方式。

40
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,760
You can keep that that's why you have to have those standards.
所以她会拒绝，并认为自己需要这样的标准。

41
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:11,360
That's why you have to know what you're going to accept and what you're not going to accept.
她觉得，自己要清楚能接受什么、不能接受什么。

42
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,800
So when things arise that are not really meant for you.
这样遇到不适合自己的事时。

43
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,720
You are not quick to be confused you are not quick to be misled.
她认为，就不会轻易迷惑或被误导。

44
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:23,120
And after I wrote that out I started to set dates when I wanted to call family and reach out to long distance friends.
写完期待后，她又安排了打电话给家人、联系远方朋友的日子。

45
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:27,120
Because sometimes it's not even that you don't have friends but your friends are spread out everywhere.
因为有时不是没有朋友，而是朋友散居在不同地方。

46
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,840
Cuz like me I went to five different high schools in the span of four years.
以她为例，四年里她上过五所不同的高中。

47
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,240
More middle and elementary schools than I can even remember.
她就读过的初中和小学更多，多到自己都记不清。

48
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,080
I have friends spread out across everywhere.
所以她的朋友分散在各地。

49
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:38,000
As you've gotten older you start having more responsibilities so many tasks to get done.
随着年龄增长，责任越来越多，要做的事情也越来越多。

50
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,400
It feels like you don't have even enough time to check in with yourself let alone family members and distant friends.
有时感觉连照顾一下自己的时间都不够，更不用说家人和远方的朋友了。

51
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,520
Text your friend like oh we should get on the phone on this day.
她建议给朋友发消息，商量在某一天打电话。

52
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:49,550
Or set reminders to call and reach out to family at least one time a month.
也可以设个提醒，至少每个月联系家人一次。

53
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:55,200
I just had one of them calls with my homegirl it gives you an opportunity to feel that reconnected with people who love you.
她刚和一位女性好友通了这样的电话，觉得这能让自己与爱自己的人重新产生联结。

54
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,760
A lot of what's wrong with our generation is we be like oh yeah the phone works both ways.
她批评自己这一代有时总说：电话又不是只能由我打，对方也能联系我。

55
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:01,680
We isolate ourselves and then wonder why we feel lonely.
她说，人们把自己孤立起来，之后又困惑为什么孤独。

56
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,950
You not going to have nobody sometimes you reach out first.
她觉得，如果总这样，身边可能就没有人了，有时候要自己先主动联系。

57
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,920
Especially if you're more on the extroverted side.
尤其当你自己比较外向时。

58
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:10,479
Actually schedule in time sit with your friends and be like every third wednesday of the month we going to chop it up.
她建议真正安排相处时间，比如约定每个月第三个星期三一起聊聊。

59
00:03:10,479 --> 00:03:13,640
Stuff like that really helps you stay connected to people.
她说，这类安排能帮助自己一直和别人保持联络。

60
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:16,630
So then when you started to feel like you got the lonely thing down.
当你觉得自己已经掌握了如何面对独处。

61
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:20,840
It's like okay I had enough I love my space I love my personal time but kaya.
你可能会说，好了，我独处够了，我喜欢自己的空间和个人时间，但是……；姓名拼写待核验。

62
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:25,640
Like I still want people I still want to be around people I still want to kick it with somebody anybody.
她模仿这种心声：我还是想见人，想有人陪，找个人一起待着也好。
